                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.4061 Motion Pictures/216: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marriner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-26T12:00:00+01:00">July 26,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 26—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>633. Reference Embassy’s telegram No. 602, July 17, 5 p.m., this year. Today’s
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Journal Officiel</hi> contains a decree dated July
                    25 putting into effect project for detaxation of cinemas and other amusements.
                    It is gratifying to note that the decree omits the Lafont amendment or any other
                    provision discriminatory against foreign films. Please repeat to Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marriner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
